{{Short description|Entry for Saudi Arabia in ISO 3166-2}}
'''ISO 3166-2:SA''' is the entry for [[Saudi Arabia]] in [[ISO 3166-2]], part of the [[ISO 3166]] [[standardization|standard]] published by the [[International Organization for Standardization]] (ISO), which defines [[code]]s for the names of the principal [[country subdivision|subdivision]]s (e.g., [[province]]s or [[state (administrative division)|state]]s) of all [[country|countries]] coded in [[ISO 3166-1]].

Currently for Saudi Arabia, ISO 3166-2 codes are defined for [[regions of Saudi Arabia|13 regions]].

Each code consists of two parts, separated by a hyphen. The first part is {{mono|SA}}, the [[ISO 3166-1 alpha-2]] code of Saudi Arabia. The second part is two digits (01&ndash;14 except 13).

